"comparison": "Both filings address the regulatory minimums for Total Loss-Absorbing Capacity (TLAC) relative to RWA. JPMorgan explicitly states its TLAC to RWA ratio requirement remained at 23.0%. Bank of America provides a breakdown of its TLAC RWA regulatory minimum, stating it consists of 18.0 percent plus a 2.5 percent TLAC RWA buffer and a 1.5 percent G-SIB surcharge, which sums to 22.0% (plus any countercyclical buffer, noted as zero). While the base totals differ slightly (23.0% vs 22.0%), both disclose the structural components of the TLAC requirement under the same regulatory framework.",
